### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal example of an HTML card that rotates 180 ° around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or animation duration to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Keeps the card centered and gives perspective */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Creates 3‑D effect */
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   The element that actually rotates */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transition: transform .6s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3‑D children */
    position: relative;
}

/* ---------- Front & Back ----------
   Two faces of the card */
.card::before,
.card::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide the back face when rotated */
    border-radius: 12px;
}

.card::before { /* Front face */
    background: linear-gradient(135deg,#ff9a9e 0%,#fad0c4 100%);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.card::after { /* Back face */
    background: linear-gradient(135deg,#a18cd1 0%,#fbc2eb 100%);
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Place it behind the front */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: bold;
}

/* ---------- Hover ----------
   Rotate the card when hovered */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card"></div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3‑D perspective so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | The rotating container. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3‑D space. |
| `::before` / `::after` | Two pseudo‑elements representing the front and back faces. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the back face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Flips the card around the Y‑axis. |

You can replace the gradient backgrounds with images, text, or any other content you like. Just remember to keep the same dimensions for both faces so they overlay perfectly. Enjoy!
